# KASAJA

Naira-first social marketplace for Nigeria connecting buyers, sellers and delivery riders.
Buy. Sell. Deliver. Connect.

**Live app:** YOUR-NETLIFY-LINK

## What runs on Arc mainnet
When a buyer confirms receipt, a Supabase Edge Function records a delivery receipt
(a hash of the order id plus a timestamp: no personal data, no funds) on Arc mainnet.

- Contract: `0x3622512fC2717B207a45Ccd0cf7dF527e818Ce8C` (Arc mainnet, chain 5042)
- Verified source: https://repo.sourcify.dev/5042/0x3622512fC2717B207a45Ccd0cf7dF527e818Ce8C/
- Example receipt transaction: https://explorer.arc.io/tx/YOUR-TX-HASH
- Source: `contracts/KasajaDeliveryReceipts.sol`, recorder logic in `supabase/functions/`

## Flow
Buyer discovers a product, messages the seller, pays in Naira (Paystack), a rider delivers,
the buyer confirms receipt, the order completes and the receipt is recorded on Arc.

## Stack
React, Vite, Tailwind, Supabase (Auth, Postgres, Realtime, Storage, Edge Functions), Paystack.

## Run locally
npm install --legacy-peer-deps
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your own values, then `npm run dev`.

## Compliance position
KASAJA is Naira-first. Rider balances are an accounting ledger, and payment protection is a
transaction release workflow. Wallet and stablecoin features will be introduced only after the
applicable Nigerian regulatory requirements are reviewed and satisfied.